  "prompt": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{5}{(2x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+3)}$ for all $x > 3$?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$(3x+14)/((2x-1)(x+3))$",
    "B": "$(3x-16)/((2x-1)(x+3))$",
    "C": "$(4x+14)/((2x-1)(x+3))$",
    "D": "$(3x+16)/((2x-1)(x+3))$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "D",
  "explanation": "Find common denominator $(2x-1)(x+3)$. Rewrite as $\\frac{5(x+3)}{(2x-1)(x+3)}-\\frac{1(2x-1)}{(2x-1)(x+3)}$. Expand numerators: $\\frac{5x+15}{(2x-1)(x+3)}-\\frac{2x-1}{(2x-1)(x+3)}$. Combine: $\\frac{(5x+15)-(2x-1)}{(2x-1)(x+3)}=\\frac{5x+15-2x+1}{(2x-1)(x+3)}=\\frac{3x+16}{(2x-1)(x+3)}$.",
